    "finding": "Both defaults ignore_errors=True; close nulls the public pointer before strict error check. Null pointer/terminal Future is not proof of native exit."
  },
  "implementation": {
    "strict": "For each known returned handle, exactly one stop(ignore_errors=False) and close(ignore_errors=False); close is attempted even after stop/control failure. No returned handle means zero native stop/close calls.",
    "unknown": "Admitted constructor without returned handle or strict close error retains owner/strong registry, UNKNOWN, no retry/eviction/replacement/resume/global ACK.",
    "stop_failure": "Successful close proves retirement; stop failure remains a safe structured error and prevents ACK/resume.",
    "not_admitted": "Only nominal preconstructor signal from MultiRoom proves no capture was admitted. USB absence/query failure before InputStream remains recoverable; postadmission None/error stays UNKNOWN.",
    "Python_work": "Actual retained callable/Future completion precedes Python work closure; borrowed executor not shut down.",
    "errors": "Retained errors carry safe descriptors. InputGroup observes cleanup and creates fresh boundary errors outside active handlers. The nominal preadmission signal is transient and discarded by the owner.",
    "hooks": "Preserve existing best-effort ordinary callback-retirement hooks; controls remain errors. Actual native closure and loop callback drains remain authoritative."
  },
